This opens an ugly can of worms. I'm changing this but it affects several other points in the code, new loop for the disabled case will be:
```
    while (!netdata_cloud_setting) {
        sleep_usec(USEC_PER_SEC * 1);
        if (netdata_exit) {
            static_thread->enabled = NETDATA_MAIN_THREAD_EXITED;
            return NULL;
        }
    }
```
But the code in `cancel_main_threads()` seems to be wrong (@mfundul please comment). If a thread *is* cancelled on the first pass we don't check if the cancel was successful, which means we wait for the status to change but there is nothing running to change it. Moving the `netdata_disable_thread_cancelability()` earlier in the thread (as @stelfrag suggests) will hide the problem in this case (as we will flip the flag and exit) but which threads in the system are being cancelled at shut-down and how does their status get updated?

Also I can see two other problems:
1. The wait to be claimed loop has the same problem.
2. The `aclk_decode_base_url` is now in the wrong place as it can be updated at claiming time.

Actually even with the change below you don't get a change to set  `static_thread->enabled = NETDATA_MAIN_THREAD_EXITED;` because cancel has already been called on the thread (`netdata_exit` is set after that cancel-threads-loop) 


```
    while (!netdata_cloud_setting) {
         sleep_usec(USEC_PER_SEC * 1);
         if (netdata_exit) {
             static_thread->enabled = NETDATA_MAIN_THREAD_EXITED;
             return NULL;
         }
     }
```

the ugly way to be able to check for `netdata_exit` is 

```
netdata_thread_disable_cancelability();
while (!netdata_cloud_setting) {
         sleep_usec(USEC_PER_SEC * 1);
         if (netdata_exit) {
             static_thread->enabled = NETDATA_MAIN_THREAD_EXITED;
             return NULL;
         }
}
netdata_thread_enable_cancelability();
```

Yes same problem with the claim loop. There is also memory cleanup issue when `goto exited` in that case (variables not allocated)

``` 
    freez(aclk_username);
    freez(aclk_password);
    freez(aclk_hostname);
    freez(aclk_port);
```

